From f11107cd5ce9dda04b6dfd6b5d5ecda1a51ae4e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 344/488] soh: name the 15 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_spot15_rrbox.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 15 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Spot15_Rrbox/z_bg_spot15_rrbox.c.

  * D_808B45C4 -> sSpawnPositions
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the fixed positions the Lon Lon crates are
    placed at, taken in turn as each one spawns.

  * D_808B4590 -> sNextSpawnIndex
    deduced, confidence HIGH: which entry of sSpawnPositions the next crate
    takes; it is bumped on each spawn and reset when the scene reloads.

  * func_808B3960 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_InitDynaPoly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: registers the crate as a dyna-poly bg actor
    with the given collision header, warning when the bg actor table is
    full.

  * func_808B3A34 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_ClearRiddenBgId
    deduced, confidence HIGH: forgets whichever bg actor the crate was last
    resting on.

  * func_808B3A40 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_IsOnRememberedBg
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns whether the crate is still sitting on
    the bg actor it remembered, by comparing their XZ positions.

  * func_808B3AAC -> BgSpot15Rrbox_CanBePushed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: decides whether a push should be allowed here:
    always inside the Lon Lon buildings, never while riding another bg
    actor, and otherwise only away from the ranch's fenced edge.

  * func_808B4010 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_IsPathBlocked
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns whether something is in the way of the
    push, by negating DynaPolyActor_IsPushPathClear at the crate's own
    width.

  * func_808B4084 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_SetupIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stops the crate dead and installs the idle
    action.

  * func_808B40AC -> BgSpot15Rrbox_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: watches for the player pushing: it starts a
    slide when the push is allowed and unobstructed, and otherwise cancels
    the player's push.

  * func_808B4178 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_SetupSlide
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the sliding action and turns gravity
    off for the slide.

  * func_808B4194 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_Slide
    deduced, confidence HIGH: accelerates the crate along the push direction
    up to 20 units, then hands off to the fall so it settles onto whatever
    is beneath it.

  * func_808B4380 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_SetupFall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: zeroes the crate's velocity, turns gravity
    back on and records the floor height before installing the falling
    action.

  * func_808B43D0 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_Fall
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drops the crate under gravity, cancels any
    push while it is airborne, and complains and recovers if it falls out of
    the world.

  * func_808B44B8 -> BgSpot15Rrbox_SetupStuck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the terminal action for a crate that
    can no longer be moved.

  * func_808B44CC -> BgSpot15Rrbox_Stuck
    deduced, confidence HIGH: refuses every push, cancelling the player's
    dyna-poly move each frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
